finding('FCR-003','Catalog route parameters escape assignment and owner authorization','CONFIRMED_DEFECT','HIGH',['stage-b/ROUND_ASSIGNMENT.json:roles.EXECUTE.route','stage-b/OWNER_DECISION_MODEL_DEVIATION.md:3-7','stage-b/run_lane.sh:194-209'],['CHILD_UNRULED_ENDPOINT/result.json'], 'An assigned EXECUTE tuple with catalog style reaches the worker stub using an owner-unruled base URL and catalog file, returns 0, and commits a clean receipt. Only style is compared; route parameters are taken from environment.','Re-derive the complete assigned route; an explicitly different governed route requires an exact owner ruling, including its parameters.','Blocks full routing-conformance claim; no network connection or upstream identity claim is made.','Child route construction','Validate catalog and base_url against the role or exact owner decision before invocation; preserve separately authorized checker backup route.')
finding('FCR-004','Containment refusal follows an in-worktree directory creation','CONFIRMED_DEFECT','MEDIUM',['user review boundary: logs/fixtures outside candidate','stage-b/run_lanes_gated.sh:34-59','stage-b/run_lane.sh:88-109'],['CHILD_JUNCTION/result.json','GATE_OS_JUNCTION/result.json','CHILD_OS_JUNCTION/result.json','GATE_OS_UNDECIDED_JUNCTION/result.json','CHILD_OS_UNDECIDED_JUNCTION/result.json'], 'Real junctions are verified by independent alias-log writes reaching fixture worktrees. Current lanes refuse containment (exit 3, zero worker calls and zero lane logs), but child mkdir already creates hgk-lanes inside the worktree. With explicit lexical shell-resolution fault injection, gate mkdir does too.','Containment admission must precede creation of an in-worktree log directory; unknown physical containment must refuse before writes.','The previous successful log-writing bypass is not reproduced; a bounded pre-refusal filesystem side effect remains.','Gate and child logdir preflight','Resolve and check the proposed destination before mkdir, then verify the created directory; test both gate and child, including physical alias and undecided resolver.')
