finding('FCR-006','Failed wrapper status query is treated as clean after record commit','CONFIRMED_DEFECT','HIGH',['ACCEPTANCE_RECORD_STAGEB.md:127-141','stage-b/run_lane.sh:16-17','stage-b/run_checker_lane.sh:46-57'],['WRAPPER_STATUS_FAILURE/result.json','REPRODUCER_READBACK.json'], 'An isolated post-commit hook creates AO12_RECORD_DIRT.txt on the wrapper record commit. An explicitly injected git -C status failure returns 128 with empty stdout. Wrapper emits CHECKER_RECORD_COMMITTED and CHECKER_BACKUP_OK, exits 0; an independent native git status exits 0 and shows the untracked dirt. Fresh replay reproduces it.','A failed cleanliness query must be unverifiable, never clean; wrapper cannot report successful committed/clean completion after an unverifiable final status.','Reopens FCR-006 postflight hygiene; the record itself is tracked, but final cleanliness is false-positive.','Checker commit_record','Check add/commit/status exit codes and enforce staged-path scope; refuse empty output from a failed status command; apply the child postflight invariants to the wrapper.')
